<title>JAPAN: Mazda Oct domestic output up 21.6% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Mazda Oct domestic output up 21.6% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mazda Motor Corp said on Wednesday its domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output in October were as follows (with percentage change from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Production	   67,272   up  21.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		 52,611   up  25.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     14,661   up   9.8 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     27,864   down 5.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		 17,940   up  15.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus	9,924   down 1.3 percent</p>
<p> Exports		36,541   up  40.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		30,090   up  37.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus	6,451   up  57.1 percent</p>
<p>Mazda's domestic vehicle production rose in October for the second successive month year-on-year, mainly helped by strong domestic demand for its new Demio compact wagon model, and higher exports, a Mazda spokesman said.</p>
<p>Domestic sales fell for the third successive month year-on-year, due to slow demand for its trucks and minivehicles, despite higher car sales.</p>
<p>Vehicle exports gained for the first time in three months on a year-on-year basis, helped by launches of Demio models in Australia and some other countries.</p>
</text>
